  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1: Setup",
  "nextTour": "2: Configure tenant settings",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Introduction",
      "description": "## Introduction \n\nIn this lab, you will learn how to protect your MCP server by requiring access tokens from authorized clients. \n\nBy the end of this lab, you will have an MCP server that:\n\n- Requires access tokens for all incoming requests.\n\n- Validates OAuth 2.0 access tokens from authorized clients.\n\n- Enforces role-based access control to manage tool permissions."
    },
    {
      "title": "Prerequisites",
      "description": "## Prerequisites\n\nIn addition to your Auth0 account, you will need to:\n\n1. Enable your tenant to use the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile.\n2. Install the Auth0 CLI to configure an Auth0 tenant for secure tool access.\n3. Install `jq` to easily parse JSON responses from the CLI.\n\nThe Auth0 CLI and `jq` have already been installed on your Codespace, so in the following step, we'll walk through how to enable Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile."
    },
    {
      "title": "Get an OpenAI API key",
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/.env.local",
      "description": "## Get an OpenAI API key\n\n1. Sign up for the OpenAI Platform here: https://platform.openai.com/signup\n2. Once signed in, go to the **API keys** section of your dashboard.\n3. Select **Create new secret key** and name your key **Auth0 labs**.\n4. Select **Create new secret key** to generate a new API key.\n5. Select the **Copy** button to copy the API key.\n6. Paste this value on the line highlighted above to set the **OPENAI_API_KEY** variable.\n\n**Note**: You must set up billing information and add a minimum credit amount to your OpenAI account or else your API calls will be rejected. You can set up billing by selecting the **gear icon** at the top right of the OpenAI Platform and going to **Billing**.\n",
      "line": 1,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 17
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 29
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable your tenant to use the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile",
      "description": "## Enable your tenant to use the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile\n\nTo use the resource parameter in your access tokens, you need to enable the Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile.\n\nThe quickest way to enable it is through the Auth0 Dashboard:\n\n1. From the Auth0 Dashboard, go to Settings on the left sidebar.\n2. Select **Advanced** in the top right corner.\n3. Scroll down to the Settings section and enable the **Resource Parameter Compatibility Profile** toggle.",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 4
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 38
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Prerequisites complete!",
      "description": "## Prerequisites complete!\n\nYou are now ready to complete this lab."
    }
  ]
}